('127.416.d.10.G',3,'Skipping a geotechnical analysis risks building on soil that cannot support the:','["weather", "brand", "structure", "calendar"]'::jsonb,2,'Soil must carry the loads.','original'),
('127.416.d.10.G',4,'Geotechnical findings can change a project''s foundation type and therefore its cost and:','["logo", "slogan", "color scheme", "schedule"]'::jsonb,3,'Subsurface conditions drive design.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.A',3,'A spread footing, a slab-on-grade, and drilled piers are all types of building:','["foundations", "windows", "roofs", "doors"]'::jsonb,0,'Foundations transfer loads to soil.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.A',4,'Deep foundations such as piles are used when the upper soils are too weak to carry the:','["trees nearby", "structure''s load", "cars passing", "tenants"]'::jsonb,1,'Deep foundations reach strong layers.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.B',3,'Forces common to structural calculations include tension, compression, and:','["fashion", "humor", "shear", "flavor"]'::jsonb,2,'Shear is a basic internal force.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.B',4,'A column supporting a floor above is mainly in:','["torsion only", "tension", "no stress", "compression"]'::jsonb,3,'Columns are squeezed.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.C',3,'The weight of the building''s own beams and floors is called the:','["dead load", "wind load", "live load", "snow load"]'::jsonb,0,'Dead load is permanent weight.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.C',4,'People, furniture, and movable equipment on a floor are the:','["seismic load only", "live load", "soil load", "dead load"]'::jsonb,1,'Live loads change.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.D',3,'A load path shows how applied loads travel through the structure down to the:','["roof only", "signs", "foundation", "windows"]'::jsonb,2,'Loads end up in the ground.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.D',4,'A floor load moves into beams, then into columns, then into the footings, so a free-body diagram helps show each:','["menu", "rumor", "paint", "reaction"]'::jsonb,3,'Diagrams track forces.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.E',3,'A simply supported beam rests on two supports and carries a load between them. The sum of the support reactions equals the:','["total applied load", "beam color", "span only", "beam name"]'::jsonb,0,'Equilibrium requires matching forces.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.E',4,'A 10-foot beam carries a 12 kip point load at midspan. Each support carries:','["12 kips", "6 kips", "24 kips", "3 kips"]'::jsonb,1,'By symmetry each takes half.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.F',3,'A shear diagram shows how the internal vertical force changes along the beam''s:','["name", "age", "length", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'Shear diagrams plot force along the span.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.F',4,'For a simply supported beam with a central point load, the maximum bending moment occurs at the:','["support", "end of the beam", "edge of the wall", "midspan"]'::jsonb,3,'Moment peaks under the load.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.G',3,'A truss is made of triangles because triangles are:','["stable shapes", "decorative only", "weak shapes", "flexible shapes"]'::jsonb,0,'Triangles resist distortion.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.G',4,'A truss that lies in one plane, like a roof truss seen from the side, is called a:','["spiral truss", "planar truss", "volume truss", "rotating truss"]'::jsonb,1,'Planar trusses are two-dimensional.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.H',3,'To find reaction forces on a truss, the engineer draws a free-body diagram of the whole truss and applies the equations of:','["grammar", "fashion", "equilibrium", "vocabulary"]'::jsonb,2,'Sum of forces and moments is zero.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.H',4,'Members of a truss are usually assumed to carry only tension or:','["shear", "bending", "torsion", "compression"]'::jsonb,3,'Truss members are two-force members.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.I',3,'Building codes dictate design loads so that structures meet a consistent minimum level of:','["public safety", "popularity", "style", "price"]'::jsonb,0,'Codes protect people.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.I',4,'Using design loads below the code minimum could make a building unsafe and is a violation of:','["marketing rules", "engineering ethics and law", "landscaping choices", "architectural taste"]'::jsonb,1,'Codes are legal requirements.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.J',3,'Structural analysis results can change member sizes, material choices, and the overall:','["phone number", "zip code", "cost", "slogan"]'::jsonb,2,'Analysis drives design.','original'),
('127.416.d.11.J',4,'If analysis shows a beam is overstressed, the engineer will most likely:','["ignore the result", "shorten the report", "remove the beam", "increase the beam size"]'::jsonb,3,'A stronger section is needed.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.A',3,'Specialties in transportation engineering include highway design, traffic operations, and:','["transit planning", "costume design", "interior design", "pastry design"]'::jsonb,0,'Transportation covers many modes.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.A',4,'A transportation engineer who times traffic signals is working in traffic:','["hydrology", "operations", "accounting", "archaeology"]'::jsonb,1,'Signal timing is operations work.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.B',3,'A Professional Transportation Planner credential shows that the holder has met standards in transportation:','["cooking", "fashion", "planning", "gardening"]'::jsonb,2,'Credentials show expertise.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.B',4,'One benefit of a transportation-specific professional credential is increased credibility with employers and:','["tourists", "competitors only", "weather agencies", "clients"]'::jsonb,3,'Credentials build trust.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.C',3,'The Institute of Transportation Engineers is a professional society that offers members training and:','["networking", "tax refunds", "parking spaces", "free fuel"]'::jsonb,0,'Societies connect professionals.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.C',4,'Attending a professional transportation conference helps an engineer learn about new standards and:','["music tours", "design practices", "menu items", "clothing lines"]'::jsonb,1,'Conferences share knowledge.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.D',3,'The length of roadway a driver needs to see an object and reach a complete halt is called:','["queue storage distance", "decision sight distance", "stopping sight distance", "passing sight distance"]'::jsonb,2,'SSD includes reaction and braking.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.D',4,'Raising the design speed of a roadway makes the needed stopping sight distance:','["drop to zero", "stay the same regardless", "shrink", "grow longer"]'::jsonb,3,'Faster vehicles need more distance.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.E',3,'Lane width, shoulder width, and curve radius are examples of roadway design:','["elements", "rumors", "costumes", "slogans"]'::jsonb,0,'Geometry affects safety.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.E',4,'A sharper curve with a smaller radius usually requires a lower:','["tax rate", "design speed", "sign color", "road name"]'::jsonb,1,'Tight curves limit speed.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.F',3,'Level of service is graded from A to F, where A represents the:','["worst conditions", "most expensive road", "best operating conditions", "longest road"]'::jsonb,2,'LOS A is free flow.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.F',4,'A roadway that operates at level of service F is experiencing:','["no vehicles", "empty lanes", "free-flowing traffic", "severe congestion"]'::jsonb,3,'LOS F means breakdown.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.G',3,'A traffic impact analysis estimates how much new traffic a development will add and its effect on nearby:','["intersections", "vacations", "parks only", "pet stores"]'::jsonb,0,'TIAs study local impacts.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.G',4,'Typical TIA components include trip generation, trip distribution, and an evaluation of the roadway''s:','["wallpaper", "capacity", "mascot", "brand voice"]'::jsonb,1,'TIAs compare demand to capacity.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.H',3,'Traffic data can be collected with tube counters, video cameras, or manual:','["menus", "lyrics", "counts", "recipes"]'::jsonb,2,'Several methods exist.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.H',4,'Pneumatic road tubes count vehicles by sensing the pulses of air created when tires:','["warm up", "rust", "pass overhead", "cross them"]'::jsonb,3,'Tubes detect axle hits.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.I',3,'A manual count records 120 vehicles in one hour. The hourly volume is:','["120 vehicles per hour", "1,200 vehicles per hour", "12 vehicles per hour", "60 vehicles per hour"]'::jsonb,0,'The count already covers one hour.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.I',4,'If a count shows 300 vehicles in 15 minutes, the equivalent hourly flow rate is:','["4,500 vehicles per hour", "1,200 vehicles per hour", "300 vehicles per hour", "900 vehicles per hour"]'::jsonb,1,'300 x 4 = 1,200.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.J',3,'The ITE Trip Generation Manual gives the number of trips a land use produces per unit such as per 1,000 square feet or per:','["tree", "sign", "dwelling unit", "school bell"]'::jsonb,2,'Trip rates depend on land use.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.J',4,'A store of 20 thousand square feet has a rate of 3 peak-hour trips per 1,000 square feet. Its peak-hour trips are:','["23", "600", "6", "60"]'::jsonb,3,'20 x 3 = 60.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.K',3,'Level of service for a road is based on measures like delay and speed relative to the road''s:','["capacity", "color", "slogan", "age"]'::jsonb,0,'LOS compares demand to capacity.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.K',4,'At a signalized intersection, level of service is often found from the average delay each vehicle experiences, measured in:','["degrees", "seconds", "pounds", "acres"]'::jsonb,1,'Delay is measured in seconds per vehicle.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.L',3,'A turn lane is warranted when the number of turning vehicles is high enough to cause delay or safety problems for the:','["pedestrian art", "utility lines", "through traffic", "parking"]'::jsonb,2,'Turn lanes remove turners from the through lane.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.L',4,'If the left-turn volume exceeds the guideline for a given opposing volume, the engineer should recommend a:','["wider sidewalk only", "stop to a dead end", "lower speed limit only", "left-turn lane"]'::jsonb,3,'Warrants justify added lanes.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.M',3,'A transportation analysis showing long delays could lead to changes in the site''s driveway locations or the:','["number of access points", "paint color", "lobby music", "owner''s name"]'::jsonb,0,'Analysis may change access.','original'),
('127.416.d.12.M',4,'A positive result from a transportation analysis helps the project win approval from the:','["social club", "city or state agency", "competing firm", "weather service"]'::jsonb,1,'Agencies review traffic studies.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.A',3,'Construction documents include design plans, specifications, and the:','["lunch menu", "staff photos", "bid forms and contract terms", "music list"]'::jsonb,2,'Documents define what is built.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.A',4,'Construction documents must be complete and clear so the contractor can build and the owner can:','["skip inspections", "change the project at will", "avoid payment", "verify compliance"]'::jsonb,3,'Documents govern construction.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.B',3,'Analysis reports for a civil project, such as drainage, geotechnical, and traffic reports, support the design:','["decisions", "jokes", "hobbies", "moods"]'::jsonb,0,'Reports justify decisions.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.B',4,'Analysis reports are submitted to reviewing agencies so they can confirm the design meets the:','["owner''s taste", "regulations", "engineer''s hobbies", "firm''s logo"]'::jsonb,1,'Agencies verify compliance.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.C',3,'A demolition sheet shows what existing features will be:','["renamed", "painted", "removed", "added"]'::jsonb,2,'Demolition sheets show removals.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.C',4,'Existing topography, property lines, and utilities appear on a demolition sheet so the contractor knows what must be protected or:','["copied", "advertised", "saved as art", "taken out"]'::jsonb,3,'Existing conditions guide removals.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.D',3,'A fire protection plan shows hydrant locations, fire lanes, and building:','["access for fire trucks", "tenant names", "bike racks only", "interior color"]'::jsonb,0,'Fire access is essential.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
