('127.416.d.13.D',4,'A fire lane must be wide enough and have a turning radius large enough for a:','["wheelbarrow", "fire apparatus", "bicycle", "sled"]'::jsonb,1,'Fire trucks need room.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.E',3,'A paving plan shows the limits of the pavement and the type of surface, such as asphalt or:','["velvet", "paper", "concrete", "wood chips"]'::jsonb,2,'Pavement types are shown.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.E',4,'A paving plan also gives pavement section details and the locations of joints and:','["art", "dances", "menus", "curbs"]'::jsonb,3,'Details guide construction.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.F',3,'A site plan that labels proposed improvements shows the locations of buildings, driveways, and:','["parking areas", "family photos", "lunch trucks", "business cards"]'::jsonb,0,'Site plans show layout.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.F',4,'A site plan must show setbacks so that reviewers can confirm the proposed buildings are placed where the code:','["forbids", "allows", "ignores", "hides"]'::jsonb,1,'Setbacks limit placement.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.G',3,'A site dimensional control plan gives measurements so the contractor can lay out buildings and curbs in the correct:','["names", "colors", "locations", "moods"]'::jsonb,2,'Control plans guide layout.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.G',4,'A dimension control plan ties building corners to fixed reference points such as property corners or survey:','["billboards", "cartoons", "menus", "benchmarks"]'::jsonb,3,'Reference points anchor layout.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.H',3,'A grading plan shows existing and proposed ground heights using contours and spot:','["elevations", "names", "logos", "colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Grading plans show heights.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.H',4,'A grading plan is designed so surface water flows away from buildings and toward drains at a minimum:','["price", "slope", "color", "width"]'::jsonb,1,'Positive drainage prevents ponding.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.I',3,'A drainage plan shows existing and proposed flow patterns, inlets, and pipes so water is directed to the:','["lobby", "roof", "outlet", "playground only"]'::jsonb,2,'Drainage plans route runoff.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.I',4,'A drainage plan may show a swale or inlet at low points to prevent water from standing on the:','["wall paint", "equipment catalog", "ceiling", "pavement"]'::jsonb,3,'Low points need inlets.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.J',3,'A utility plan shows the locations of water lines, sewer lines, and electric and gas lines that serve the:','["site", "weather", "bank", "calendar"]'::jsonb,0,'Utility plans show services.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.J',4,'On a utility plan, proposed and existing utilities are shown with different line styles so the contractor can tell what is:','["pretty versus ugly", "new versus old", "hot versus cold", "loud versus quiet"]'::jsonb,1,'Line styles communicate status.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.K',3,'An erosion control plan identifies best management practices, such as silt fences and construction:','["trophies", "logos", "entrances", "parties"]'::jsonb,2,'BMPs keep sediment on site.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.K',4,'A stabilized construction entrance reduces the amount of mud that trucks carry onto:','["school buses only", "parking meters", "private offices", "public roads"]'::jsonb,3,'Entrances shed mud.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.L',3,'A quality control review finds errors and conflicts in the plans before they are issued for:','["construction", "a game", "a vacation", "a party"]'::jsonb,0,'QC prevents costly mistakes.','original'),
('127.416.d.13.L',4,'A QC reviewer who is not the original designer is more likely to catch mistakes because of a fresh:','["password", "perspective", "lunch", "paycheck"]'::jsonb,1,'Independent review finds more errors.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.A',3,'A bid tabulation lists each item''s description, quantity, unit, unit price, and:','["owner", "slogan", "extended price", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'Extension = quantity x unit price.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.A',4,'A bid item of 500 linear feet of pipe at 30 dollars per foot has an extended price of:','["530 dollars", "150 dollars", "1,500 dollars", "15,000 dollars"]'::jsonb,3,'500 x 30 = 15,000.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.B',3,'Comparing a bid tabulation with the construction documents ensures every item in the plans appears in the:','["bid", "menu", "poster", "playlist"]'::jsonb,0,'Missing items cause cost surprises.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.B',4,'If a bidder leaves out a pay item that appears in the plans, the engineer should flag the bid as:','["perfect", "incomplete", "finalized", "lowest by default"]'::jsonb,1,'Complete bids include every item.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.C',3,'To create a bid tabulation for a project, the engineer lists all pay items and the bids from each:','["journalist", "tourist", "contractor", "competitor''s cousin"]'::jsonb,2,'Tabs organize bid results.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.C',4,'The total bid is found by adding the extended prices of all the:','["signatures", "pages", "bidders", "bid items"]'::jsonb,3,'Totals sum the items.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.D',3,'The project manual contains the bidding requirements, contract forms, and the:','["technical specifications", "lunch order", "vacation photos", "staff gossip"]'::jsonb,0,'The manual bundles documents.','original'),
('127.416.d.14.D',4,'Organizing a project manual in the standard order helps bidders find the information they need to prepare an accurate:','["dinner", "price", "alarm", "playlist"]'::jsonb,1,'Organization helps bidders.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.A',3,'A manager who compares completed tasks with the schedule is tracking whether team goals and project:','["logos are on time", "colors are matching", "milestones are being met", "cars are parked"]'::jsonb,2,'Tracking shows progress.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.A',4,'If a milestone is missed, the manager should find the cause and adjust the:','["milestone''s name", "office carpet", "uniforms", "plan"]'::jsonb,3,'Tracking supports correction.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.B',3,'One effective method for resolving conflict on a project team is to listen to each person and focus on the:','["problem, not the person", "oldest member", "person, not the problem", "loudest voice"]'::jsonb,0,'Constructive conflict focuses on issues.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.B',4,'When two engineers disagree about a design choice, a good first step is to compare each option to the:','["time of day", "project requirements", "weather forecast", "office mood"]'::jsonb,1,'Requirements provide an objective basis.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.C',3,'Leaders who communicate clear goals and recognize good work help team members stay:','["isolated", "bored", "motivated", "confused"]'::jsonb,2,'Leadership shapes morale.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.C',4,'A project leader who ignores team input risks lower team member:','["salary", "age", "height", "engagement"]'::jsonb,3,'People disengage when unheard.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.D',3,'Evaluating a teammate''s performance should be based on specific, observable:','["contributions", "guesses", "appearances", "rumors"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence-based feedback is fair.','original'),
('127.416.d.15.D',4,'Effective performance feedback names what was done well and what could be done to:','["hide", "improve", "delay", "punish"]'::jsonb,1,'Balanced feedback helps growth.','original'),
('127.416.d.16.A',3,'The Texas Engineering Practice Act regulates who may offer engineering services and requires a:','["uniform", "logo", "license", "mascot"]'::jsonb,2,'The Act protects the public.','original'),
('127.416.d.16.A',4,'Offering engineering services to the public in Texas without being licensed can result in:','["promotions", "rewards", "tax credits", "penalties"]'::jsonb,3,'Unlicensed practice is illegal.','original'),
('127.416.d.16.B',3,'Texas Administrative Code Chapter 137 includes rules of conduct for engineers that require them to hold paramount the public''s:','["safety, health, and welfare", "comfort", "entertainment", "opinion"]'::jsonb,0,'Rules put safety first.','original'),
('127.416.d.16.B',4,'An ethical case study may describe an engineer who was pressured to approve a faulty design. The best response under the code is to:','["approve quietly", "refuse and report", "delete the report", "blame a coworker"]'::jsonb,1,'Duty to the public overrides pressure.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.A',3,'Using recycled steel, reclaimed wood, or low-carbon concrete are examples of sustainable building:','["fashions", "songs", "materials", "captions"]'::jsonb,2,'Sustainable materials reduce impact.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.A',4,'Designing a building to use daylight and well-insulated walls is a sustainable method that reduces:','["window area to zero", "tenant count", "site size", "energy use"]'::jsonb,3,'Efficient design cuts energy.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.B',3,'LEED is a program that certifies buildings designed to meet defined standards for:','["sustainability", "size", "location only", "decoration"]'::jsonb,0,'LEED rates green performance.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.B',4,'Envision is a rating system used for sustainable civil projects such as roads, pipelines, and:','["sports bars", "water systems", "clothing stores", "office lobbies"]'::jsonb,1,'Envision covers infrastructure.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.C',3,'A project that earns a sustainability certification may qualify for incentives and attract tenants who value:','["noise", "waste", "green buildings", "delays"]'::jsonb,2,'Certification can add value.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.C',4,'Pursuing certification typically adds documentation requirements and design effort, which can affect the project''s:','["address", "mascot", "slogan", "cost and schedule"]'::jsonb,3,'Certification has trade-offs.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.D',3,'Design choices such as adding trees and permeable pavement can improve air quality and reduce:','["stormwater runoff", "property lines", "building codes", "traffic signs"]'::jsonb,0,'Green features help the environment.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.D',4,'Indoor air quality, lighting, and acoustics are design factors that affect human:','["tax rates", "health and comfort", "office hours", "street names"]'::jsonb,1,'Design shapes well-being.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.E',3,'Construction dust, noise, and runoff can affect the health of workers and nearby:','["calendars", "statues", "residents", "coupons"]'::jsonb,2,'Construction has impacts.','original'),
('127.416.d.17.E',4,'A contractor who covers stockpiles and wets disturbed soil is limiting airborne:','["paint", "music", "light", "dust"]'::jsonb,3,'Dust control protects health.','original'),
('127.417. d.1',3,'A consulting engineer learns that a client''s building plan skips a required fire exit to save money. Ethics requires her to:','["insist on the code-required exit", "let the client decide alone", "quietly omit the exit", "stamp it as is"]'::jsonb,0,'Public safety outranks client cost wishes.','original'),
('127.417. d.1',4,'An engineer discovers an error in a bridge calculation she already sealed. The ethical action is to:','["blame the software", "notify the client and correct it", "say nothing", "wait for an inspection"]'::jsonb,1,'Honesty about errors protects the public.','original'),
('127.417. d.2.A',3,'A transit agency wants shorter bus waits. Writing down exactly what delays buses is the design process step of:','["buying the buses", "choosing a mascot", "defining the problem", "picking a paint color"]'::jsonb,2,'A well-defined problem comes first.','original'),
('127.417. d.2.A',4,'Defining an engineering problem carefully matters because a solution to the wrong question will:','["need no testing", "save money", "win awards", "waste time and money"]'::jsonb,3,'Wrong problem, wrong solution.','original'),
('127.417. d.2.B',3,'In the research stage, a team designing a bike path gathers crash records, user counts, and existing:','["design guidelines", "song lyrics", "menu prices", "jersey colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Research collects relevant data.','original'),
('127.417. d.2.B',4,'Reviewing how other cities built protected bike lanes helps a team learn what has and has not:','["been funded by tourists", "worked in practice", "been advertised", "been named"]'::jsonb,1,'Precedents guide design.','original'),
('127.417. d.2.C',3,'Brainstorming ten ways to cool a plaza, such as shade sails, trees, and misters, is called:','["inspection", "depreciation", "ideation", "closeout"]'::jsonb,2,'Ideation generates options.','original'),
('127.417. d.2.C',4,'Turning the shade-sail idea into a sketch with dimensions and materials moves the team from ideation to:','["abandonment", "litigation", "retirement", "conceptualization"]'::jsonb,3,'Concepts develop ideas into rough designs.','original')
